config BR2_PACKAGE_IPOD_GADGET
	bool "ipod-gadget"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Out-of-tree Linux USB gadget kernel modules that make the board
	  enumerate to a host (a car head unit, a dock) as an Apple iPod:
	  a USB Audio Class 1 streaming interface plus a HID interface that
	  carries iAP (iPod Accessory Protocol) packets on a /dev/iap0
	  character device.

	  Builds three modules, loaded in this order:
	    g_ipod_audio  - creates the "iPodUSB" ALSA playback card
	    g_ipod_hid    - HID transport for iAP
	    g_ipod_gadget - the composite device tying them together

	  The matching userspace iAP client is the separate "ipod" package.

	  https://github.com/oandrew/ipod-gadget

comment "ipod-gadget needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
